      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds both incredible and terrifying. if this really is a \"feedback loop\" like you're saying, i'm worried about what happens when the loop gets too strong. like, if i'm interfacing with the grid, could i accidentally draw too much power *into* myself? i don't want my own nervous system to get fried by a surge from the building. \n\nhow would i even tell the difference between my own discharge and a surge coming from the external wires? is there a way to \"map\" the direction of the flow so i know if the energy is moving out from me or into me?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
